00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.980
{=0}2.43: Seiin High School Boys Volleyball Team

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:35.770
<i>What should we do?</i>
<i>We're not used to facing adversity</i>

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:40.900
<i>So our resolve's definitely not all there</i>

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.310
<i>Back then, we were just</i>

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.650
<i>Envious of others and</i>

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:50.350
<i>Angry at something we couldn't see</i>

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.940
<i>We just kept glaring at the next step</i>

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:55.310
<i>That we could've easily taken</i>

00:01:55.310 --> 00:02:00.270
<i>And it was eating away at us silently</i>

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.060
<i>We were so scared that we went numb</i>

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.480
<i>And our legs buckled from under us</i>

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:11.350
<i>We still can't forget the tears</i>
<i>that fell back then even now</i>

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:16.150
<i>Even though we're so frail we might break,</i>
<i>we still continued to seek love</i>

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:21.270
<i>We don't want to forget the reason</i>
<i>we're standing on this stage</i>

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:26.060
<i>Because you're the one who made me stronger</i>

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:30.520
<i>I give you this lovely ballad</i>
<i>within this beautiful attack</i>

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.690
Sweet! I'm on a roll.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.560
Haijima! One more!

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.650
We're done. Let's clean up.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:55.110
Aw. Just three… Just one more.

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:58.270
I keep looking at their #7. It's like
looking at me from two years ago.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:01.150
Their #8's totally controlling him.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:05.730
If their #8 stops functioning,
that whole team is going down.

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:08.020
Why would they leave so much to a first year?

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.100
Ochi.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.480
Do you want to go to the center court
at the Spring Tournament?

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:19.150
Do you want to go to the center court
at the Spring Tournament?

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:23.850
Say, Subaru. Why are you
so obsessed with that phrase?

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.900
Whatever, just keep saying it.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:30.270
Until I make you the manager on
the Spring Tournament's center court.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.690
Why, though?

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.900
Think of it as my
good luck charm and just say it.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.810
Good luck charm?

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.480
Say it, Mitsuomi.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:46.600
O-Of course I want to go.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:47.810
You better make me a manager

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.940
that gets to stand on the center court
at the Spring Tournament.

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:56.480
Cheering for you guys on the bench
at the Spring Tournament is my dream.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:57.980
All right!

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:02.020
In that case, let me take care
of some possible competition.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:05.900
This other genius from Fukui.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.260
Episode 7: 'The Ruling Hero of the Court'

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.720
Fukuho                          Seiin

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.150
Got it!

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.990
Fukuho                          Seiin

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:51.350
Fukuho                          Seiin

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:53.850
So far, we've been totally equal.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:57.940
Hopefully, we can get a break when
Subaru's up front on the third rotation.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:58.940
Yes.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.600
They got a break?

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:13.900
A waterfall...

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:18.520
This is the 23rd side out in a row? Seriously?

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:18.500
Fukuho                          Seiin

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:22.230
That was good! Don't panic and cut them off!

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.400
How many is that for Subaru?

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.150
He's hit 11 and scored nine.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.260
Hits

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.260
Points

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.600
Kohei's not getting any better.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:38.850
He's not the strongest mentally.
We need to raise his spirits somehow.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:39.850
Touch!

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:46.810
Free ball!

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:59.770
Haijima's even better than expected.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:02.810
I think we're getting the ball
to Subaru too much.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:05.980
Well, he's planning on hitting even more.

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:07.150
Get the ball to me!

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:10.440
Touch!

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:14.730
It's best to keep getting the ball to Subaru

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:17.900
to keep the other team from taking the flow.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:20.980
But that's putting too much on Subaru.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.270
And he'll figure it out.

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:30.980
He's Fukuho's ace.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.620
Fukuho                          Seiin

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:35.810
Oda and Kanno can attack from the back.

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:38.230
Which one will Haijima use?

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:45.810
That's a powerful dump!

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:48.850
They got us. We weren't even considering that.

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:52.350
He's ambidextrous and can
hit that hard with his left...

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:53.810
That's gonna be tricky.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.100
Bring it to the left!

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.190
We're counting on you, Subaru!

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:09.810
Yes!

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.530
Fukuho                          Seiin

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:14.310
We got the break!

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:15.440
Yeah!

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:22.650
Now, who's next?

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:27.900
Yes!

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:29.340
Fukuho                          Seiin

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.230
He got through.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:30.350
Yes!

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:31.090
Subaru!

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:32.230
Subaru- <i>senpai</i> !

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:33.480
Way to go, Subaru!

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:35.810
You're awesome, Subaru- <i>senpai</i> !

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:38.350
Way to go, Subaru!

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:56.350
I see...

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:59.270
So that's the Demon Bazooka...

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:00.350
Touch!

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:05.580
Yu!

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:06.520
Got it!

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:09.560
Slam it, Kohei!

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:15.480
Yeah!

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:15.590
Fukuho                          Seiin

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.190
Damn...

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:19.940
Nice!

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:22.100
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:28.020
I'm done for today.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:33.020
I'll leave the rest to Kohei.
I've already talked to the coach.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:38.270
Hey, that last set...
You didn't need to go that hard.

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:40.770
I've got something I need to protect.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:45.440
I'm Fukuho's captain and ace,
and the prefectural MVP.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:51.150
I need to take everyone who's counting
on me to the center court at nationals.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:55.650
Our seniors that didn't make it
to the center court, our team,

00:08:55.650 --> 00:09:00.100
their families, and you and the coach.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:04.100
I've got so many things
I have to protect. It's sorta insane.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.600
You're carrying too much.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:11.480
That responsibility and people
counting on me is what gives me strength.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:16.810
I have this overwhelming amount of energy
that they'll never get their hands on.

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:18.980
Those newbies will never get that.

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:22.020
That's why I'm not going to lose to anyone.

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:26.100
Kohei!

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:28.650
Show them what we're made of!

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:30.440
Give it all you've got!

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:32.350
Yeah! All right!

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:35.060
Come on! Let's do this!

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:38.230
He gets so discouraged easily and can be a pain,

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:41.560
but I'm glad he's also
super easy to pick back up.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:44.520
You're seriously something, you know that?

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:48.690
Don't let them lure you over!
Two blockers on the left!

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:50.440
Yeah! All right!

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:55.060
Thank you very much!

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:58.810
We both took three sets each.
I guess it's a tie today.

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:01.600
I'm gonna take it as you let us have three sets.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:03.520
We've got plenty to work on.

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:05.690
To work on, huh?

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:07.850
Can't wait until we play you guys at the finals.

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:11.900
Well, look at you. You're talking like
you're gonna make it there for sure.

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:13.100
Of course.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:15.730
Then we'll be waiting for you.

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:20.980
#8!

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:24.020
See ya later.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:31.980
He could at least smile sometime.
What's his name again?

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:34.060
Haijima...

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:35.850
Kimichika Haijima.

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:40.230
Subaru Mimura...

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.400
Five more days until the prefectural qualifiers.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:51.940
We can't let Oda- <i>senpai</i> and Aoki- <i>senpai</i>

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:55.270
retire until we make it
to the real deal in January.

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:56.730
You're sure taking this lightly.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:11:01.400
When we go up against Fukuho, you're gonna
be head-to-head with Subaru Mimura.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:04.020
I mean, he's amazing and all,

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:10.100
but I don't get this sense of despair
that he's totally undefeatable.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:12.730
You didn't feel a sense of despair?

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:16.850
E-Er, you're telling me to improve
before getting that confident, right?

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:19.850
Yeah. You need to get better
and catch up to him.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:22.020
Catch up to him by November.

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:25.060
First, we're gotta get through the
first round of the qualifiers this weekend.

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:25.900
Right.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:29.190
We have to win three matches
before we even play Fukuho.

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:29.830
Right.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.270
We know.

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:33.060
Thanks, Kuroba.

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:33.630
Huh?

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:37.310
Let me stay the captain until January.

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:40.850
I-If you heard me, I wish you
would've said something sooner.

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:41.770
Oda.

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:43.150
Hey.

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:44.020
What's up?

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:47.650
I'd like you to sit out
the match against Fukuho.

00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:50.150
Haijima, what the hell did you just--

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:52.900
I said I'd like Oda to sit out
of the match against Fukuho.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:57.230
Does that mean I'll be
taking Oda- <i>senpai</i> 's place?

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:59.440
During our practice match with Fukuho,

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:02.730
they kept hitting the ball above Oda.

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:06.730
Next time, they're going
to aim for you even harder.

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:09.850
Considering all of the members of Fukuho
are tall enough to play at nationals,

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:11.850
it's going to be rough to have Oda up front.

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:16.150
And it's your job to figure out
how to get around that.

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:18.730
We can attack in various ways.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:21.520
But there's nothing I can do
about someone's physical height

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:23.150
when it comes to blocking.

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:25.310
W-W-Wait.

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:28.520
But if we take Oda- <i>senpai</i> out and
the strength of our attack goes down,

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:30.150
what's the point?

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:32.600
I'll make up for the lost attack power.

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:36.940
Uchimura, you're being given
a chance to play a game,

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.810
so why aren't you taking it?

00:12:38.810 --> 00:12:40.560
How can you stand warming the bench

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:43.520
when first years are on the starting lineup?

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:45.730
Are you determined to do everything you can

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:49.100
to take back your place on the starting lineup?

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:52.730
If you are, I'll do everything I can, as well.

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:04.020
You told me before, Oda.

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:08.650
That you want to play volleyball
even a day, or even a second longer.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:11.810
And you wanted me to help you do that.

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:16.730
Does that mean even if you're
off the court for the team?

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:20.730
Or were you saying that, putting yourself first?

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:27.150
Um... we'd expect switching out
Uchimura and Kuroba,

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:31.520
but we haven't really switched Uchimura
and Oda- <i>senpai</i> out much before.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:35.600
I think we should do everything
we can to perfect everything we know.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:38.310
I'm talking about the match against Fukuho.

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:41.230
We still have two months before
the finals, so that's plenty of time.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:46.400
Then you probably didn't need
to bring this up now, Haijima.

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:48.230
We're five days from the qualifiers.

00:13:48.230 --> 00:13:51.650
You didn't need to throw
everyone for a loop like this.

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:56.650
Having Oda- <i>senpai</i> sit out
isn't just a physical issue.

00:13:56.650 --> 00:14:00.440
It's also taking away our mental
and emotional backbone.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:07.600
But... we should try this at the qualifiers.

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:10.310
What's wrong?

00:14:10.310 --> 00:14:12.020
You boys not going to practice?

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:14.560
Oh, sorry.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:17.900
Guys, I'll talk this over with the coach.

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:21.350
I get what Haijima's trying
to say, and I'll consider it.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:23.350
I'll hear what you have to say, too, Uchimura.

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:27.440
So come by later. You good with that, Aoki?

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:29.520
You're the captain.

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:33.350
Haijima. Let me answer your question later.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:36.850
I don't know the answer right now.

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:41.440
I want to be absolutely sure
when I give you my answer.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:45.810
We've been talking too long.
Let's hurry up and get that net up.

00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:48.730
Haijima, you...

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:52.480
I... wasn't...

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:56.940
There're better ways to say that, you dumbass.

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:05.150
Um, Uchimura- <i>senpai</i> .

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:06.560
What's up, Kuroba?

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:09.600
Uh, um, well...

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:18.190
Uchimura- <i>senpai</i> , so what happened
with the conversation earlier?

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:20.810
Are we just gonna throw it out?

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.560
So that is what you wanted to talk about.

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.600
No, I just...

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:31.310
I was just wondering if you really
didn't want to do everything you could

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:34.650
just like Haijima was saying.

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:39.810
The genius players who go on those documentaries

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:41.600
have the balls to say,

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:46.020
"If I can do it, anyone can do it
with a little bit of hard work."

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:48.230
Like hell, I can!

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:52.480
Sure they think they're being humble,
but that's a genius's pride.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:57.520
Being able to push yourself
to the limits is a skill all on its own.

00:15:57.520 --> 00:16:00.600
When people don't understand that,
they ask for a lot,

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:02.270
expecting that it can be done with hard work.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:05.150
That's why people think Haijima's a pain.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:09.060
You just sit there listening,
but you don't get it either.

00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:10.230
You're still at the point

00:16:10.230 --> 00:16:12.810
where you feel like you can keep growing
as long as you keep trying, right?

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:17.060
So you tried to come over here
asking me if I wasn't going to

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:19.350
at least try to do everything that I could.

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:21.270
I-I wasn't...

00:16:21.270 --> 00:16:23.400
But you were, dummy.

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:29.100
I mean, you're not the brightest,
so you're easy to talk to, at least.

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:32.020
I don't think Haijima's ever gonna get it,

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:34.980
so you need to at least get this in your head.

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:40.020
If we lose Oda- <i>senpai</i> 's guard,
you're the only one who can back him up.

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:44.060
At this rate, if he goes somewhere else
like that, he's gonna get crushed.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:48.400
E-Even I don't plan on backing him up forever.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.900
Huh, I see.

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:54.600
Just so you know, I'm not saying
I'm not gonna do my best.

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:58.980
Of course, I'm gonna try after being
called out in front of everyone like that.

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:06.900
And just like Oda- <i>senpai</i> , I adore you guys.

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:10.150
I'm not gonna try to crush
our promising first years.

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:14.400
Haijima, why are you in such a rush?

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:15.520
What's wrong?

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:18.230
Someone's calling me from home.

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:20.980
Grandma got hurt?

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:20.720
Faculty Room

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:24.100
She's in the hospital? How is she?

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:27.940
She'll be out in two or three days? I see.

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.850
Huh? Why?

00:17:29.850 --> 00:17:31.600
I'll go over there, too!

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:33.770
Huh? Kuroba?

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:38.230
Okay, I will.

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:40.100
Okay, bye.

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:43.730
Haijima, what about me?

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:46.060
They told me to go to your place for today.

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:47.150
Huh?!

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:57.650
Have Kuroba- <i>sensei</i> let you
stay at their place until Sunday.

00:17:57.650 --> 00:17:59.940
You have an important match
coming up, don't you?

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:03.810
This was a request from Kiminobu.

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:06.520
My dad? He said something?

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:13.190
He asked your grandmother
and I to take care of you.

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:17.230
Kiminobu was filled with regret.

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:22.020
He didn't know why he didn't realize
what you were going through sooner

00:18:22.020 --> 00:18:24.520
when that incident happened
at your middle school.

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:34.060
Kuroba, do you have a sec?

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:36.150
What?

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:38.850
What's up?

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:42.190
Well, um...

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:45.940
When my gramps said that my dad regretted

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:49.900
what happened with me in middle school, I...

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:53.350
Are you actually coming to me for advice?!

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:55.100
Never mind!

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:56.480
Wait, my bad.

00:18:56.480 --> 00:19:00.850
The middle school thing?
You mean with Sota, right?

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:05.650
I don't think I was wrong with
what I told Sota and the others.

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:10.980
So the fact that my dad had regrets is a bit...

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:13.190
So you don't like the fact
that your dad has regrets

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:16.770
about something you don't feel you did wrong?

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:19.350
I pointed out very obvious things to work on

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:22.350
and said the best way for us to win.

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:23.650
Because that's the best way

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:29.020
to get Oda to stand on the court
at the Spring Tournament.

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:32.900
Listen. We all know that.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:36.850
We can trust you on the decisions
you make in volleyball.

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:39.690
I'm pretty sure Oda- <i>senpai</i> knows that, too.

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:43.940
But we want to make it to
the Spring Tournament, right?

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:49.270
If not, I won't be able to stay on this team.

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:51.600
Seriously...

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:53.600
If we know what's wrong with the team

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:57.230
but aren't willing to fix it,
that's even weirder.

00:19:57.230 --> 00:20:00.150
I'm not wrong here.

00:20:01.270 --> 00:20:07.020
But then... Why do I feel this... regret?

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:10.100
I'm not sure if it's actually regret.

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:15.190
Or if it's the same regret my dad felt or not.

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:20.730
What the hell? Are you listening?

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:25.650
Seriously, what am I even going to do with you?

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:30.940
What do you mean? Damn it, now I don't
know what I wanted to say anymore.

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:33.020
I know! Subaru Mimura!

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:33.940
What?

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:37.020
The key's Subaru Mimura.

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:39.940
You're telling me to be like him? Seriously?

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:41.480
No.

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:45.600
First off, Mimura's a hitter
and you're a setter.

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:47.900
I'm the hitter here.

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:51.980
The two of us together make
a pretty good pair, don't we?

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:56.400
So the two of us together just
need to be like Subaru Mimura.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:21:02.520
I mean, he's two years older than us,
so we can compensate with the both of us.

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:06.850
Look, you need to catch up
to Subaru Mimura on your own.

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:08.350
You need to catch up to him and surpass him.

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:10.730
Don't just raise the bar suddenly.

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:15.150
And when did this conversation become
about us instead of me? You dumbass.

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:18.270
You guys from Tokyo sure know
how to make insults sting.

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:24.650
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:21:26.230 --> 00:21:31.850
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:40.690
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:44.730
<i>The azure world smiles upon me</i>

00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:57.060
<i>The knife made up of words from my friend</i>

00:21:57.060 --> 00:22:04.020
<i>Still lingers inside my head today</i>

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:10.190
<i>You glared up at the clouds high in the sky</i>

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:16.650
<i>And near your house, the horizon undulated</i>

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:24.100
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:22:25.730 --> 00:22:31.230
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:40.150
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:22:40.150 --> 00:22:48.350
<i>The azure world stabs me strongly in the back</i>

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:51.050
